 "chunks": [
  {
   "text": "When sigma is one or less, the arrows don't shrink fast enough,",
   "start": 0.7,
   "end": 4.175
  },
  {
   "text": "and the sum never settles.",
   "start": 4.175,
   "end": 5.963
  },
  {
   "text": "Think of one, plus x, plus x squared, and so on.",
   "start": 5.963,
   "end": 9.875
  },
  {
   "text": "It only works between minus one and one,",
   "start": 9.875,
   "end": 12.325
  },
  {
   "text": "but it clearly wants to be one over one minus x,",
   "start": 12.325,
   "end": 15.425
  },
  {
   "text": "which makes sense everywhere except x equals one.",
   "start": 15.425,
   "end": 18.6
  },
  {
   "text": "In the same way, zeta has exactly one extension to the whole plane that stays",
   "start": 19.575,
   "end": 23.988
  },
  {
   "text": "complex-differentiable, its analytic continuation,",
   "start": 23.988,
   "end": 27.538
  },
  {
   "text": "everywhere but s equals one.",
   "start": 27.538,
   "end": 29.688
  },
  {
   "text": "Here it is.",
   "start": 29.688,
   "end": 30.837
  },
  {
   "text": "Color shows the direction of zeta's value, and each ring doubles its size.",
   "start": 30.837,
   "end": 35.675
  },
  {
   "text": "Where all the colors meet at a dark point, zeta is zero.",
   "start": 35.675,
   "end": 39.125
  }
 ],
